@startuml fork-decision-flow
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #E8F0FE
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #4285F4
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF9C4
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #FBC02D

title Decision: Direct Merge vs .patch File

start

:Feature is stable on feature branch;

:Does it touch files
already in PATCHED_FILES?;

if (yes) then (yes)
  :**Must use .patch file**
  Direct merge would be
  silently reverted by
  the sync workflow;
  stop
else (no)
endif

:Does it touch files
upstream changes frequently?
(e.g. gotypes.d.ts, settingsconfig.go);

if (yes) then (yes)
  :**Use .patch file**
  Avoids recurring merge
  conflicts on every sync;
  stop
else (no)
endif

:Is it a large feature
(many files, ongoing iteration)?;

if (yes) then (yes)
  :**Use .patch file**
  Easier to maintain,
  regenerate from feature branch;
  stop
else (no)
  :**Direct merge is fine**
  Small, isolated changes
  won't conflict with upstream
  ``git checkout dev.patch``
  ``git merge feature/xxx``
  ``git push``;
  stop
endif

@enduml
